There's no existing project in the directory. Since you mentioned you have an existing project, I'll provide the implementation you can drop into it. Here's what you need:

**1. Create `Middleware/ApiExceptionHandler.cs`:**

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Diagnostics;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;

namespace YourApp.Middleware;

internal sealed class ApiExceptionHandler(ILogger<ApiExceptionHandler> logger)
    : IExceptionHandler
{
    public async ValueTask<bool> TryHandleAsync(
        HttpContext httpContext,
        Exception exception,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var (statusCode, title) = exception switch
        {
            KeyNotFoundException => (StatusCodes.Status404NotFound, "Not Found"),
            ArgumentException   => (StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest, "Bad Request"),
            InvalidOperationException => (StatusCodes.Status409Conflict, "Conflict"),
            _ => (0, (string?)null)
        };

        if (statusCode == 0)
            return false; // falls through to default handler → 500 with no details

        logger.LogWarning(exception, "Handled API exception: {Title}", title);

        httpContext.Response.StatusCode = statusCode;
        await httpContext.Response.WriteAsJsonAsync(new ProblemDetails
        {
            Status   = statusCode,
            Title    = title,
            Detail   = title,   // safe; never expose exception.Message
            Instance = httpContext.Request.Path
        }, cancellationToken);

        return true;
    }
}
```

**2. Wire it up in `Program.cs`:**

```csharp
// ── Services ──
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<ApiExceptionHandler>();
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();   // RFC 7807 for unhandled (500) too

// ── Middleware (order matters) ──
app.UseExceptionHandler();     // catches exceptions globally
app.UseStatusCodePages();      // converts bare status codes to Problem Details
```

**How it works:**

| Exception | Status | Exposed detail |
|---|---|---|
| `KeyNotFoundException` | 404 | `"Not Found"` |
| `ArgumentException` | 400 | `"Bad Request"` |
| `InvalidOperationException` | 409 | `"Conflict"` |
| Anything else | 500 | Generic — no stack trace or message leaked |

The `IExceptionHandler` pipeline runs before the default handler. When `TryHandleAsync` returns `false` (unrecognized exceptions), the built-in `AddProblemDetails()` handler produces a safe 500 response automatically — no sensitive details included.

Your endpoints stay clean with no try-catch:

```csharp
app.MapGet("/api/items/{id}", (int id, IItemService svc, CancellationToken ct) =>
{
    // Just throw; the middleware handles the rest
    var item = svc.GetById(id) ?? throw new KeyNotFoundException();
    return TypedResults.Ok(item);
});
```
